---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Open Russian grammatical error correction research at synterr-nlp."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <section style="margin: 1.5rem 0 3rem;">
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.6;">
      synterr-nlp is an open research effort on Russian grammatical error
      correction. We build tools and benchmarks that make it possible to
      evaluate language models honestly: rule by rule, against the
      prescriptive grammar that defines the rules, with reproducible
      pipelines and full data provenance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin: 3rem 0;">
    <h2>What we work on</h2>
    <p>
      Existing GEC benchmarks for Russian summarize heterogeneous behavior
      into one F-score and miss the parts where models silently regress.
      Our research program addresses this in three ways:
    </p>
    <ol style="margin: 1rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.65;">
      <li>
        <strong>A rule-grounded taxonomy.</strong> 98 fine-grained error tags
        anchored in Rozental's reference grammar, mapped against existing
        Russian GEC corpora to surface what they cover and what they don't.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Synterr, a synthetic-error generator.</strong> Configurable
        per-rule rates, dependency-tree-driven handlers (agreement,
        government, punctuation), with morpheme-level corruption that
        respects Russian morphology.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Per-rule diagnostics.</strong> Browsable tables and
        evaluation harnesses that surface rule-level model behavior aggregate
        metrics hide.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section style="margin: 3rem 0;">
    <h2>Team</h2>
    <ul class="team-list">
      <li>
        <span class="member-name">Anna Smirnova</span>
        <span class="member-aff">HEC Lausanne, University of Lausanne</span>
        <span class="member-link"><a href="mailto:anna.smirnova@unil.ch">anna.smirnova@unil.ch</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="member-name">Artyom Kopan</span>
        <span class="member-aff">Saint Petersburg State University</span>
        <span class="member-link"><a href="mailto:artyom.kopan@gmail.com">artyom.kopan@gmail.com</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="member-name">Vladislav Makeev</span>
        <span class="member-aff">Saint Petersburg State University</span>
        <span class="member-link"><a href="mailto:makeev.vladislav.d@gmail.com">makeev.vladislav.d@gmail.com</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="member-name">George Chernishev</span>
        <span class="member-aff">Saint Petersburg State University</span>
        <span class="member-link"><a href="mailto:chernishev@gmail.com">chernishev@gmail.com</a></span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section style="margin: 3rem 0;">
    <h2>Acknowledgments</h2>
    <p>
      Compute provided on the DGX Spark hosted by Simon Scheidegger at HEC Lausanne.
      The site, the synterr code, and several paper figures use Claude assistance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin: 3rem 0;">
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Bugs and feature requests:
      <a href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr/issues" rel="external">GitHub Issues</a>.
      Contributions: see <a href="/synterr/contributing/">the contributing guide</a>.
      Press, collaborations, anything else: email
      <a href="mailto:anna.smirnova@unil.ch">Anna</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  p { line-height: 1.6; }

  .team-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .team-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr 14rem;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .member-name {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .member-aff {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .member-link {
    text-align: right;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .team-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
    .member-link { text-align: left; }
  }
</style>
